---
import TextPage from '../layouts/TextPage.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---

<TextPage
  title="Contact"
  description="Get in touch with the Men Women Psychology editorial team — corrections, source suggestions, and questions are all welcome."
  canonical="/contact"
  intro="We read everything. Corrections and source suggestions are especially welcome."
>
  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p>
    The best way to reach us is by email at
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We aim to reply within a few business days.
  </p>

  <h2>What to send</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Corrections.</strong> If you believe a page misstates a finding or cites something
      inaccurately, tell us which page and what is wrong. Where possible, include the source.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Source suggestions.</strong> Know a strong study we should reference? Send it. We
      prioritize peer-reviewed research and well-established frameworks.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Topic requests.</strong> There is a question you wish we covered? Let us know — reader
      questions shape what we write next.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>General feedback.</strong> Tone, clarity, balance — we want this to be genuinely
      useful and genuinely fair to everyone.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we handle corrections</h2>
  <p>
    Accuracy is the whole point of this site, so corrections get priority. If you flag a factual
    error or a misused citation, we check it against the original source. If you are right, we fix
    the page and update its "last reviewed" date; if the picture is more nuanced, we will explain
    our reasoning. Either way, we would rather be accurate than be right, and we are grateful to
    anyone who helps us get closer to the truth. You can read how we choose and weigh sources on our
    <a href="/research-methodology/">research methodology</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2>Response times</h2>
  <p>
    We are a small editorial team, so replies usually take a few business days. Corrections and
    source suggestions tend to get the fastest turnaround because they are the easiest to act on. If
    your message is time-sensitive, say so in the subject line and we will do our best to prioritize
    it.
  </p>

  <h2>A note on personal advice</h2>
  <p>
    We are not able to offer personalized relationship, psychological, or clinical advice over
    email. Men Women Psychology is an educational resource, not a counseling service, and a general
    article can never substitute for support tailored to your specific situation. If you are going
    through something difficult, a licensed professional — a therapist, counselor, or your doctor —
    can help in a way we cannot. If you are in crisis, please contact a local emergency service or
    crisis line right away.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    If you email us, we use your message only to respond to you. We do not add you to marketing
    lists. See our <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> for the full picture.
  </p>
</TextPage>
